@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] native-tour-copies-use-the-active-source
Home and ReviewSession MUST share one tour-copy adapter for the active opaque
sourceStorageNamespace. The private versioned file layout MUST contain no raw server,
account, Access credential or pull name in its paths. A source change MUST revoke
pending writers before deleting that active namespace; a retired handle MUST NOT
read or restore it. Ordinary scene destruction MUST preserve valid files for verified
reopening. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS source ownership, cached-first
continuity and same-adapter plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] native-tour-files-are-atomic-bounded-and-recoverable
Native tour copies MUST retain the original TourResult head and generated time,
write atomically and keep at most the existing 200 newest files across source
namespaces. Files MUST be limited to four MiB and the retained directory to sixty-four
MiB. Missing, malformed, empty or oversized copies MUST remain recoverable through
the real server. Activation MUST reconcile an interrupted write's excess before
reading; an unchanged generated tour MUST NOT need a rewrite to recover the budget.
File writes MUST be serialized in submission order and source
invalidation MUST fence them before any replacement writer. Source: the accepted
21 Oct 2026 iOS private-cache budget/corruption plan and existing Android TourStore.
